{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8605f7ee", "timestamp": "2026-10-10T14:19:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug about incorrect dependency mapping in FlowForce has been resolved. You can check the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/FlowForce/pull/40.", "utterranceID": "20261010-0-6e12b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261010-0-6e12b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71071933", "timestamp": "2026-10-10T14:22:00", "text": "Great news, @eid_8605f7ee! Can you explain what caused the issue?", "utterranceID": "20261010-1-875f2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261010-1-875f2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8605f7ee", "timestamp": "2026-10-10T14:25:00", "text": "Sure, George. The root cause was a flaw in the dependency analysis algorithm. It wasn't accurately tracing and mapping the interdependencies between API components, which led to incorrect maps.", "utterranceID": "20261010-2-4d981"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261010-2-4d981"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_9a7b2132", "timestamp": "2026-10-10T14:29:00", "text": "Thanks for the update, Julia. How did you manage to fix it?", "utterranceID": "20261010-3-88ebf"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261010-3-88ebf"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8605f7ee", "timestamp": "2026-10-10T14:31:00", "text": "I updated the algorithm to include a more comprehensive traversal method that correctly identifies and maps all relevant API components. This ensures that the dependency maps reflect the true structure and flow of the APIs.", "utterranceID": "20261010-4-b6956"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261010-4-b6956"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e5e36dc1", "timestamp": "2026-10-10T14:34:00", "text": "Awesome work, Julia! This should help users get a clearer picture of their API flows.", "utterranceID": "20261010-5-6d0b6"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261010-5-6d0b6"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8605f7ee", "timestamp": "2026-10-10T14:39:00", "text": "Thanks, Alice! If anyone encounters any further issues, please let me know.", "utterranceID": "20261010-6-ce4bc"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261010-6-ce4bc"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-fbc815"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71071933", "timestamp": "2026-10-10T14:42:00", "text": "Will do, thanks again for the quick turnaround, Julia!", "utterranceID": "20261010-7-dd5af"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261010-7-dd5af"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8605f7ee", "timestamp": "2026-07-10T14:34:00", "text": "Okay, I've gone through the changes. The data handling updates look solid, but I noticed that the user consent mechanisms could be more explicit. We might need to add more detailed consent options for users to align with GDPR requirements. What do you think, @eid_71071933?", "utterranceID": "20260712-4-1cbf9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260712-4-1cbf9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71071933", "timestamp": "2026-07-10T14:35:00", "text": "I agree with Julia. The consent mechanisms are a bit generic. We should provide users with more granular control over their data. Also, I noticed the compliance documentation could use a bit more detail on the new processes. @eid_4e8b2cdc, could you expand on that section?", "utterranceID": "20260712-5-dbdab"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260712-5-dbdab"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4e8b2cdc", "timestamp": "2026-07-10T14:38:00", "text": "Thanks for the feedback, both of you! I'll work on making the consent options more detailed and update the documentation accordingly. Appreciate the insights! 🙌", "utterranceID": "20260712-6-a5262"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260712-6-a5262"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8605f7ee", "timestamp": "2026-07-10T14:41:00", "text": "No worries, @eid_4e8b2cdc! Once you've made those changes, just ping us again. It's looking good overall, just needs those tweaks. 😊", "utterranceID": "20260712-7-037eb"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260712-7-037eb"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71071933", "timestamp": "2026-07-10T14:44:00", "text": "Exactly, @eid_4e8b2cdc. Let us know when you're ready for another round of review. Thanks for tackling this important task!", "utterranceID": "20260712-8-7f275"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260712-8-7f275"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71071933", "timestamp": "2026-07-14T05:43:00", "text": "Hi team, I wanted to discuss some open-source features that might give us insights for our Kafka integration. Let's see how others are handling similar challenges. 😊", "utterranceID": "20260713-0-770b7"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260713-0-770b7"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71071933", "timestamp": "2026-07-14T05:47:00", "text": "First up, Apache Flink has a PR titled 'Integrate Pulsar for Enhanced Stream Processing'. They are using Apache Pulsar to boost stream processing and cut down latency. Here's the link: https://github.com/apache/flink/pull/3319. Thoughts? 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260713-1-b9bf4"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260713-1-b9bf4"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_f2474622", "timestamp": "2026-07-14T05:48:00", "text": "@eid_71071933 That's interesting! Pulsar is known for its multi-tenancy and geo-replication features. It might be worth considering if we need those capabilities in the future. But for now, Kafka's ecosystem seems more mature for our needs.", "utterranceID": "20260713-2-30e5a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260713-2-30e5a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8605f7ee", "timestamp": "2026-07-14T05:53:00", "text": "I agree with George M. Pulsar is cool, but Kafka's community support and tooling are hard to beat. Still, it's good to know what Flink is doing. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260713-3-50c35"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260713-3-50c35"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_71071933", "timestamp": "2026-07-14T05:57:00", "text": "Great points! Next, let's look at Apache Spark's PR 'Real-Time Data Ingestion with RabbitMQ'. They're adding RabbitMQ for real-time data ingestion. Check it out here: https://github.com/apache/spark/pull/3320.", "utterranceID": "20260713-4-3af2e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260713-4-3af2e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8605f7ee", "timestamp": "2026-07-14T06:02:00", "text": "RabbitMQ is solid for message queuing, but I think Kafka's partitioning and scalability are more aligned with our goals. Spark's approach is interesting, though. 🤓", "utterranceID": "20260713-5-3f597"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260713-5-3f597"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_294ba09d", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:00:00", "text": "Hi team, I've found some interesting open-source bugs that might help us with our current Salesforce issues. Let's take a look at them together! 😊", "utterranceID": "20261116-0-f682a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-0-f682a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_294ba09d", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:04:00", "text": "First, we have a bug in Grafana titled 'Incorrect Data Aggregation in Dashboard Panels'. It seems similar to our 'Incorrect Data Aggregation in Summary Views' issue. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/1537. Ian, what do you think? Could this provide some insights for our problem?", "utterranceID": "20261116-1-b2d70"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-1-b2d70"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d098d618", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:07:00", "text": "Thanks, Alice! This Grafana issue does seem quite similar to what we're seeing. I'll review the PR to see how they approached the fix. It might give us some ideas on how to tackle our data aggregation problem. 👍", "utterranceID": "20261116-2-3640c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-2-3640c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_294ba09d", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:10:00", "text": "Great! Next up is a bug in Kibana titled 'Delayed Data Refresh in Visualizations'. This aligns with our 'Delayed Data Refresh in Real-Time Dashboards' issue. Check out the PR here: https://github.com/elastic/kibana/pull/1538. Charlie, could you take a look and see if there's anything we can learn from their approach?", "utterranceID": "20261116-3-96548"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-3-96548"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0d918f1", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:12:00", "text": "Sure thing, Alice! I'll dive into the Kibana PR and see how they handled the refresh delays. Hopefully, it will shed some light on our dashboard refresh issue. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20261116-4-54e6f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-4-54e6f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_294ba09d", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:15:00", "text": "Awesome, thanks! Lastly, there's a PostgreSQL bug titled 'Data Loss During High-Volume Transactions'. This is quite similar to our 'Data Loss During High-Volume Transactions' issue. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/postgres/postgres/pull/1539. Ian, since you're already looking into our data loss issue, could you also review this one?", "utterranceID": "20261116-5-d177e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-5-d177e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d098d618", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:19:00", "text": "Absolutely, Alice. I'll check out the PostgreSQL PR and see if their solution can be adapted to our situation. I'll keep everyone posted on what I find. 💪", "utterranceID": "20261116-6-c282b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-6-c282b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_294ba09d", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:23:00", "text": "Thanks, Ian and Charlie! Let's keep these open-source solutions in mind as we work on our fixes. Feel free to reach out if you need any help or want to discuss further. Let's get these issues resolved! 🙌", "utterranceID": "20261116-7-5df7b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-7-5df7b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0d918f1", "timestamp": "2026-11-17T04:26:00", "text": "Will do! Thanks for coordinating, Alice. Let's get to work! 🔧", "utterranceID": "20261116-8-5353b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261116-8-5353b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0d918f1", "timestamp": "2026-11-18T09:51:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug titled 'Delayed Data Refresh in Real-Time Dashboards' has been resolved. You can check out the details in the PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/FlowForce/pull/48.", "utterranceID": "20261118-0-c65a8"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261118-0-c65a8"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-alicemartinez-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b3b2e4"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d0d918f1", "timestamp": "2026-11-18T09:53:00", "text": "The root cause was a bottleneck in the data synchronization process between the API flow optimizer and the visualization module. It wasn't optimized for real-time data streams, which led to the delays.", "utterranceID": "20261118-1-46d0f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261118-1-46d0f"}

