{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iansmith-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-1c7f59"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_b4d260c1", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T05:28:00", "text": "@eid_5782059f Agreed! Kafka's approach to streaming could help us scale our feedback loop. We should consider how they manage data throughput and latency. ⚡", "utterranceID": "20261018-7-032cc"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261018-7-032cc"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iansmith-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-1c7f59"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_ecaa9084", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T05:31:00", "text": "I like the idea of using a stream processor. It could help us maintain a continuous flow of data, which is crucial for real-time analytics. Let's keep this in mind as we design our system. 🔄", "utterranceID": "20261018-8-3f0e5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261018-8-3f0e5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iansmith-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-xtaix-1c7f59"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_01942cf0", "timestamp": "2026-10-19T05:35:00", "text": "Finally, we have Scikit-learn's Interactive Model Refinement. It adds a mechanism to refine models based on user feedback and interaction data, enhancing prediction accuracy. Here's the link: https://github.com/scikit-learn/scikit-learn/pull/2706.", "utterranceID": "20261018-9-779a1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261018-9-779a1"}
