{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_88c661bc", "timestamp": "2026-05-20T02:43:00", "text": "Smart index rebalancing sounds like exactly what we need! As our data grows, maintaining performance is crucial. PostgreSQL's approach could provide a solid foundation for our own indexing improvements. 📈", "utterranceID": "20260519-8-5260d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260519-8-5260d"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliataylor-TrendForce", "channelID": "ch--daix-db3e57"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_ecaa9084", "timestamp": "2026-05-20T02:46:00", "text": "Agreed, Emma. Rebalancing indexes dynamically could prevent a lot of performance issues down the line. We should definitely explore this further. Maybe George can take a closer look at how they implemented it? 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260519-9-969cd"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260519-9-969cd"}
