{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-27cdca"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4988ee2a", "timestamp": "2026-08-01T17:50:00", "text": "Hi team, I was looking into some open-source projects that have implemented TLS 1.3, and I think they could provide some valuable insights for our PR. Let's discuss them! 😊", "utterranceID": "20260801-0-c8934"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260801-0-c8934"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-27cdca"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_0aa9f1f7", "timestamp": "2026-08-01T17:51:00", "text": "Sounds great, Emma! What did you find?", "utterranceID": "20260801-1-64054"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260801-1-64054"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-27cdca"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4988ee2a", "timestamp": "2026-08-01T17:53:00", "text": "First up, Apache Kafka has a PR titled 'Implement TLS 1.3 for Broker Communication'. It focuses on enhancing security by integrating TLS 1.3 for encrypted communication between Kafka brokers. Here's the link: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/4888", "utterranceID": "20260801-2-4e853"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260801-2-4e853"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-27cdca"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7dfbbca2", "timestamp": "2026-08-01T17:54:00", "text": "Interesting! @eid_4988ee2a, I think the way Kafka handles broker communication could be quite similar to how we manage our internal services. It might be worth looking into their approach to see if we can adopt any of their strategies. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260801-3-9db8c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260801-3-9db8c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-27cdca"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4988ee2a", "timestamp": "2026-08-01T17:59:00", "text": "Good point, Ian D.! I'll dive deeper into their implementation and see what we can learn from it. Next, I found a PR from Nginx titled 'Support for TLS 1.3 in HTTP/2 Connections'. This one adds TLS 1.3 support to improve security and performance for HTTP/2 connections. Check it out here: https://github.com/nginx/nginx/pull/4889", "utterranceID": "20260801-4-6824e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260801-4-6824e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-27cdca"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_0aa9f1f7", "timestamp": "2026-08-01T18:00:00", "text": "Nginx is always a good reference for performance improvements. Their focus on HTTP/2 could give us some ideas on optimizing our handshake processes. Maybe we can adapt some of their techniques for our use case. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260801-5-5f98c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260801-5-5f98c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-27cdca"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4988ee2a", "timestamp": "2026-08-01T18:04:00", "text": "Absolutely, Ian G.! I'll make a note to explore their performance enhancements further. Lastly, OpenSSL has a PR titled 'Optimize Handshake Performance with TLS 1.3'. It introduces optimizations for faster handshake processes using TLS 1.3. Here's the link: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/4890", "utterranceID": "20260801-6-6ef12"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260801-6-6ef12"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-27cdca"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7dfbbca2", "timestamp": "2026-08-01T18:08:00", "text": "OpenSSL's optimizations could be crucial for us, especially if we're aiming for improved handshake performance. @eid_4988ee2a, maybe you could look into how they achieved these optimizations and see if we can apply similar techniques. 🔍", "utterranceID": "20260801-7-9846d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260801-7-9846d"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_9f13e9bc", "timestamp": "2026-05-20T17:35:00", "text": "Finally, Grafana has a PR called 'Visualization Recommendation Experiments'. They set up an A/B testing system to evaluate different visualization recommendations for better data insights. Here's the link: https://github.com/grafana/grafana/pull/3834. Ian, any thoughts?", "utterranceID": "20260520-7-2febc"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260520-7-2febc"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7dfbbca2", "timestamp": "2026-05-20T17:39:00", "text": "Grafana's focus on recommendation experiments aligns closely with our goals. Their system for evaluating recommendations could provide a solid foundation for our framework. We should definitely dive deeper into their implementation. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260520-8-eb01a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260520-8-eb01a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_619c8be2", "timestamp": "2026-05-20T17:43:00", "text": "Agreed, Ian. Grafana's approach might help us streamline our recommendation engine. Let's keep this one on our radar. 📌", "utterranceID": "20260520-9-5a298"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260520-9-5a298"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_9f13e9bc", "timestamp": "2026-05-20T17:45:00", "text": "Awesome feedback, team! I'll take a closer look at these projects and see how we can incorporate some of their strategies into our A/B testing framework. I'll keep you all posted. Thanks for the input! 🙌", "utterranceID": "20260520-10-7841a"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260520-10-7841a"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_9f13e9bc", "timestamp": "2026-05-22T15:46:00", "text": "Hi team, please check my PR for the A/B Testing Framework implementation: https://github.com/salesforce/VizForce/pull/5. This sets up the foundational framework for experimentation with different visualization recommendations. I've integrated a third-party A/B testing library and set up initial test cases. Let me know your thoughts! 😊", "utterranceID": "20260524-0-3997c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260524-0-3997c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7dfbbca2", "timestamp": "2026-05-22T15:47:00", "text": "Hey @eid_9f13e9bc, thanks for sharing! I'll take a look at it now. Excited to see how this will enhance our visualization recommendations! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260524-1-fedc5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260524-1-fedc5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_619c8be2", "timestamp": "2026-05-22T15:50:00", "text": "Checking it out now, @eid_9f13e9bc! This is going to be a game-changer for our experiments. 🔍", "utterranceID": "20260524-2-a1d17"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260524-2-a1d17"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7dfbbca2", "timestamp": "2026-05-22T15:51:00", "text": "Alright, I've gone through the PR. The A/B testing framework is integrated nicely and seems operational within the VizForce environment. The initial test cases are clear and can be toggled on/off for different user segments. Great job on the documentation too, it's very clear on how to add new A/B tests. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260524-3-f1bee"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260524-3-f1bee"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_619c8be2", "timestamp": "2026-05-22T15:55:00", "text": "I agree with Ian. Everything looks solid, and the documentation is super helpful. The framework is well-integrated, and the test cases are easy to manage. @eid_9f13e9bc, you've covered all the acceptance criteria. 🎉", "utterranceID": "20260524-4-3a2af"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260524-4-3a2af"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7dfbbca2", "timestamp": "2026-05-22T15:59:00", "text": "LGTM, approved! Let's get this merged and start experimenting! 🥳", "utterranceID": "20260524-5-a3cc5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260524-5-a3cc5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_619c8be2", "timestamp": "2026-05-22T16:03:00", "text": "Approved from my side too! Great work, @eid_9f13e9bc! Can't wait to see the results from our first tests. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260524-6-56e88"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260524-6-56e88"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionamiller-VizForce", "channelID": "ch-force-a7e9a5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_9f13e9bc", "timestamp": "2026-05-22T16:05:00", "text": "Thanks, @Ian Davis and @Hannah Johnson! Appreciate the quick review and feedback. I'll merge it now. Let's make some data-driven magic happen! ✨", "utterranceID": "20260524-7-1cb30"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260524-7-1cb30"}

