{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iandavis-ExplainabilityForce", "channelID": "ch-inaix-b0fd52"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e0273792", "timestamp": "2026-10-28T08:26:00", "text": "Hi team, I wanted to kick off a discussion about our new PR for integrating authentication and authorization into our GraphQL API. I've found some similar features in open-source projects that might give us some insights. Let's dive in! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20261027-0-3c489"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-0-3c489"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iandavis-ExplainabilityForce", "channelID": "ch-inaix-b0fd52"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e0273792", "timestamp": "2026-10-28T08:31:00", "text": "First up, we have a feature from the Django project. They've integrated OAuth2 authentication for their REST API. You can check it out here: https://github.com/django/django/pull/3799. This could be relevant since OAuth2 is a widely adopted standard for securing APIs.", "utterranceID": "20261027-1-7e9ee"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-1-7e9ee"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iandavis-ExplainabilityForce", "channelID": "ch-inaix-b0fd52"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_0528f388", "timestamp": "2026-10-28T08:36:00", "text": "@eid_e0273792 OAuth2 is definitely something we should consider. It's robust and well-supported. Plus, it could make our API more appealing to developers who are already familiar with it. What do you think, Charlie?", "utterranceID": "20261027-2-337cd"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-2-337cd"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iandavis-ExplainabilityForce", "channelID": "ch-inaix-b0fd52"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_1f17ef52", "timestamp": "2026-10-28T08:39:00", "text": "I agree, Bob. OAuth2 could be a great fit. It might require some additional setup, but the benefits in terms of security and user management are worth it. Let's keep this in mind as we move forward. 👍", "utterranceID": "20261027-3-641d1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-3-641d1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iandavis-ExplainabilityForce", "channelID": "ch-inaix-b0fd52"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e0273792", "timestamp": "2026-10-28T08:41:00", "text": "Great points, both of you! Next, let's look at Node.js. They've implemented Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) for their HTTP server: https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/3800. This allows for fine-grained access control based on user roles.", "utterranceID": "20261027-4-6a1bf"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-4-6a1bf"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iandavis-ExplainabilityForce", "channelID": "ch-inaix-b0fd52"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_0528f388", "timestamp": "2026-10-28T08:43:00", "text": "RBAC is interesting. It could give us the flexibility to define different levels of access for different users. This might be particularly useful if we have complex user hierarchies. What do you think, @eid_1f17ef52?", "utterranceID": "20261027-5-a5a88"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-5-a5a88"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iandavis-ExplainabilityForce", "channelID": "ch-inaix-b0fd52"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_1f17ef52", "timestamp": "2026-10-28T08:48:00", "text": "Absolutely, Bob. RBAC could be a game-changer for us. It aligns well with our need for granular access control. We should definitely consider how we can incorporate similar functionality.", "utterranceID": "20261027-6-ab8d5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-6-ab8d5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-iandavis-ExplainabilityForce", "channelID": "ch-inaix-b0fd52"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e0273792", "timestamp": "2026-10-28T08:51:00", "text": "Finally, there's a feature from Apache Kafka. They've added SASL authentication to Kafka Streams: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/3801. This ensures that only authenticated clients can produce or consume messages.", "utterranceID": "20261027-7-d94e2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261027-7-d94e2"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_86f94a48", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T07:06:00", "text": "Great points, @eid_01e37306 and Julia! Next, let's look at Hasura. They've implemented a GraphQL engine to handle real-time data queries and mutations. Here's their PR: https://github.com/hasura/graphql-engine/pull/4883. What do you think? 🤓", "utterranceID": "20260726-4-10243"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260726-4-10243"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T07:07:00", "text": "Hasura's real-time capabilities are impressive. Their use of subscriptions for real-time data could be a game-changer for us, especially if we want to offer live updates. We should definitely consider this. 🔄", "utterranceID": "20260726-5-24049"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260726-5-24049"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_86f94a48", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T07:10:00", "text": "Absolutely, Emma. Real-time data handling is becoming more crucial. I'll take a closer look at how Hasura implements this and see if we can adapt some of their strategies. 🕵️‍♂️", "utterranceID": "20260726-6-ba07e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260726-6-ba07e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_86f94a48", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T07:12:00", "text": "Lastly, we have GraphQL Yoga. They've initialized a server to streamline API request handling and execution. Check out their PR here: https://github.com/dotansimha/graphql-yoga/pull/4884. Any thoughts on this one? 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260726-7-75e2b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260726-7-75e2b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_724e1180", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T07:13:00", "text": "GraphQL Yoga is known for its simplicity and ease of use. It might be a good option if we want something lightweight and easy to integrate. Plus, their focus on developer experience is a big plus! 🌟", "utterranceID": "20260726-8-7f7ef"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260726-8-7f7ef"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_01e37306", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T07:17:00", "text": "I agree with Julia. Yoga's simplicity could help us get up and running quickly. It might not have all the bells and whistles of Apollo or Hasura, but it could be a good starting point. 🏃‍♀️", "utterranceID": "20260726-9-39112"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260726-9-39112"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_86f94a48", "timestamp": "2026-07-27T07:22:00", "text": "Thanks for the input, everyone! 🙌 I'll dive deeper into these projects and see how we can incorporate some of their best practices into our setup. Let's aim to make our GraphQL server as efficient and user-friendly as possible. 💪", "utterranceID": "20260726-10-30768"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260726-10-30768"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_86f94a48", "timestamp": "2026-07-29T08:41:00", "text": "Hi team, please check my PR for setting up the GraphQL server for CollaborateForce: https://github.com/salesforce/CollaborateForce/pull/8. This PR initializes the server to handle API requests, ensuring it can process queries and mutations effectively. Let me know your thoughts! 😊", "utterranceID": "20260731-0-ae884"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260731-0-ae884"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_01e37306", "timestamp": "2026-07-29T08:44:00", "text": "@eid_86f94a48 Thanks for sharing! I'll start reviewing it now. Excited to see how the GraphQL setup looks! 🔍", "utterranceID": "20260731-1-84d35"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260731-1-84d35"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_724e1180", "timestamp": "2026-07-29T08:48:00", "text": "Hey @eid_86f94a48, I'll take a look at it too. Setting up GraphQL is a great step forward for us! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260731-2-ee4eb"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260731-2-ee4eb"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-bobbrown-CollaborateForce", "channelID": "ch-force-de9cfb"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_446bc3ee", "timestamp": "2026-07-29T08:52:00", "text": "Checking it out now, @eid_86f94a48! Let's see how it integrates with our current systems. 🤓", "utterranceID": "20260731-3-c8a40"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260731-3-c8a40"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliadavis-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-38c82b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7b2a9f4a", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T15:19:00", "text": "Hey everyone, yes, the product team has decided to take a different approach, which might make this schema unnecessary. We should discuss if reverting is the best option.", "utterranceID": "20260915-1-a9344"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260915-1-a9344"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliadavis-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-38c82b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_31ca5b45", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T15:23:00", "text": "Can someone clarify what the new product direction is and how it affects the GraphQL schema?", "utterranceID": "20260915-2-b4f3f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260915-2-b4f3f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliadavis-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-38c82b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_9e0ce30d", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T15:25:00", "text": "The new direction focuses more on REST APIs for customer profiles instead of GraphQL, so this schema might not be needed anymore.", "utterranceID": "20260915-3-65700"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260915-3-65700"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliadavis-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-38c82b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4de5cd7f", "timestamp": "2026-09-15T15:30:00", "text": "If we don't need the schema, reverting seems like the logical step. But are there any parts of the schema that could still be useful?", "utterranceID": "20260915-4-b7f91"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260915-4-b7f91"}
