{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8605f7ee", "timestamp": "2026-06-04T02:48:00", "text": "@George Martinez, the Kafka PR seems quite relevant. Improving throughput and latency is exactly what we're aiming for. I think we could learn a lot from their approach to stream processing. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260603-1-c5a2c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260603-1-c5a2c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-alicedavis-FlowForce", "channelID": "ch-ceaix-1deacc"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_399e4119", "timestamp": "2026-06-04T02:50:00", "text": "Agreed, Julia. The Kafka team's focus on optimizing algorithms could definitely provide some insights. We should consider how their changes might apply to our architecture. 📈", "utterranceID": "20260603-2-56fa3"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260603-2-56fa3"}
