{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliadavis-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-38c82b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_f66c3942", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T17:32:00", "text": "Hi team, I wanted to discuss some open-source features that might help us with our GraphQL API's authentication and authorization. Let's see what we can learn from them! 😊", "utterranceID": "20261024-0-ac4f9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-0-ac4f9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliadavis-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-38c82b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_f66c3942", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T17:35:00", "text": "First up, we have a feature from Node.js: Secure JWT Authentication Middleware. It implements a middleware for handling JWT authentication to enhance API security. You can check it out here: https://github.com/nodejs/node/pull/3646. Thoughts? @eid_8a2cd06b", "utterranceID": "20261024-1-b11ae"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-1-b11ae"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliadavis-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-38c82b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8a2cd06b", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T17:37:00", "text": "Thanks, David! This could be really useful for us. JWT is pretty standard for securing APIs, and having a middleware approach could simplify our implementation. It might be worth considering how they handle token expiration and refresh. 👍", "utterranceID": "20261024-2-94001"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-2-94001"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-juliadavis-PitchForce", "channelID": "ch--paix-38c82b"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_c5bce3e8", "timestamp": "2026-10-24T17:40:00", "text": "Agreed, Fiona. JWT is robust, and integrating it as middleware could streamline our process. We should definitely look into how they manage token storage and validation. @eid_f66c3942, maybe you could dive deeper into this?", "utterranceID": "20261024-3-4bcb8"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20261024-3-4bcb8"}

