{"title": "Fix Security Vulnerability in Parameter Adjustment Module by Adding Authentication Checks", "summary": "### Summary
This pull request addresses a security vulnerability in the Parameter Adjustment Module where unauthorized users could manipulate model parameters due to missing authentication and authorization checks.

### Changes Made
- Implemented authentication and authorization checks on all endpoints within the parameter adjustment module.
- Refactored the endpoint logic to ensure secure access control.
- Updated unit tests to cover new authentication logic and ensure no unauthorized access is possible.

### Testing
- Conducted manual testing to verify that unauthorized users cannot access or manipulate model parameters.
- Ran automated test suite to ensure all existing functionality remains intact and new security measures are effective.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/AutoTuneForce/pull/51", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "True", "number": "51", "state": "closed", "user": {"login": "eid_961f0487"}, "created_at": "2027-01-27T03:21:00", "reviews": [{"state": "APPROVED", "user": {"login": "eid_8c71a7a9"}, "comment": "The changes look good to me. The implementation of authentication checks effectively addresses the security vulnerability. I have reviewed the code and tested the functionality, and everything works as expected. Approved for merge.", "submitted_at": "2027-01-27T02:43:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_AutoTuneForce_pull_51"}

