{"title": "Fix Immediate Triggering of Indexing Process After Data Updates", "summary": "### Summary
This pull request addresses the issue of outdated search results in SearchForce due to delays in updating the search index after data changes in the database.

### Changes Made
- Implemented an immediate trigger for the indexing process whenever data updates occur in the database.
- Refactored the indexing service to ensure it listens for database change events and initiates the indexing process without delay.

### Testing
- Conducted unit tests to verify that the indexing process is triggered immediately after data updates.
- Performed integration tests to ensure that the search index reflects the latest database state promptly.
- Monitored the system for any performance impacts and confirmed that the changes do not introduce any regressions.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/SearchForce/pull/32", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "True", "number": "32", "state": "closed", "user": {"login": "eid_4eec2a5a"}, "created_at": "2027-03-02T22:58:00", "reviews": [{"state": "APPROVED", "user": {"login": "eid_6d14c4ec"}, "comment": "Looks great! The changes effectively address the indexing delay issue, and the tests confirm that the fix works as expected. Approved for merge.", "submitted_at": "2027-03-02T21:06:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_SearchForce_pull_32"}

