{"Channel": {"name": "develop-hannahmiller-SecurityForce", "channelID": "ch-force-6a73a1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d7acdc4c", "timestamp": "2026-07-01T21:24:00", "text": "Totally agree, Hannah. Efficient data handling is key for us. I’ll review their data ingestion methods and see what we can learn. Thanks for the input, everyone! I’ll compile my findings and we can discuss further in our next meeting. 😊", "utterranceID": "20260701-8-3cb35"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260701-8-3cb35"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-hannahmiller-SecurityForce", "channelID": "ch-force-6a73a1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_d7acdc4c", "timestamp": "2026-07-04T01:07:00", "text": "Hi team, please check my PR for integrating the Threat Intelligence APIs with our existing systems: https://github.com/salesforce/SecurityForce/pull/8. This should ensure seamless data flow and maintain current functionalities. Let me know your thoughts! 😊", "utterranceID": "20260707-0-8ec95"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260707-0-8ec95"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-hannahmiller-SecurityForce", "channelID": "ch-force-6a73a1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_b9189afb", "timestamp": "2026-07-04T01:12:00", "text": "Thanks for sharing, @eid_d7acdc4c! I'll take a look at it now. Excited to see how the integration is shaping up. 🔍", "utterranceID": "20260707-1-922b9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260707-1-922b9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-hannahmiller-SecurityForce", "channelID": "ch-force-6a73a1"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_f50066b1", "timestamp": "2026-07-04T01:14:00", "text": "Hey @eid_d7acdc4c, I'll review it too. Looking forward to seeing those new capabilities in action! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260707-2-355ba"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260707-2-355ba"}

{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6d14c4ec", "timestamp": "2027-03-17T18:14:00", "text": "Great! Next, there's a bug in GIMP titled 'Font Scaling Inconsistencies'. It's about inconsistent font scaling on high-DPI displays causing layout issues and text overlap in the UI. Check out the PR here: https://github.com/GNOME/gimp/pull/1743. George, this might be useful for the UI issue you're handling.", "utterranceID": "20270317-3-2ad5c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270317-3-2ad5c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_12c203a5", "timestamp": "2027-03-17T18:17:00", "text": "Thanks, David! I'll take a look at how they addressed the scaling issues. It might give us some insights into fixing our mobile UI problems. 📱", "utterranceID": "20270317-4-59417"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270317-4-59417"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6d14c4ec", "timestamp": "2027-03-17T18:20:00", "text": "Awesome! Lastly, there's a bug in spaCy titled 'Contextual Drift in Long Queries'. The NLP model returns partially relevant results for long text inputs, affecting search accuracy. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/explosion/spaCy/pull/1744. Julia, this seems to align with the NLP issue you're investigating.", "utterranceID": "20270317-5-5a896"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270317-5-5a896"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_b20b58ad", "timestamp": "2027-03-17T18:25:00", "text": "Absolutely, David! I'll dive into their solution to see if we can enhance our context handling for long queries. 🤖", "utterranceID": "20270317-6-d51a5"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270317-6-d51a5"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6d14c4ec", "timestamp": "2027-03-17T18:28:00", "text": "Thanks, everyone! Let's keep these references in mind as we work on our fixes. Feel free to reach out if you need any help or want to discuss further. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20270317-7-187f4"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270317-7-187f4"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4eec2a5a", "timestamp": "2027-03-17T18:33:00", "text": "Will do! I'll update you all on any relevant findings from the Elasticsearch PR. 🔐", "utterranceID": "20270317-8-8970f"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270317-8-8970f"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_12c203a5", "timestamp": "2027-03-17T18:37:00", "text": "Same here, I'll share any useful insights from the GIMP issue. 👍", "utterranceID": "20270317-9-20e93"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270317-9-20e93"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_b20b58ad", "timestamp": "2027-03-17T18:42:00", "text": "I'll keep you posted on the spaCy findings. Thanks, team! 🙌", "utterranceID": "20270317-10-b2562"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270317-10-b2562"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4eec2a5a", "timestamp": "2027-03-23T06:24:00", "text": "Hi team, the bug about improper access control in query execution has been resolved. You can check the details in the approved PR here: https://github.com/salesforce/SearchForce/pull/33.", "utterranceID": "20270322-0-76d84"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270322-0-76d84"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_12c203a5", "timestamp": "2027-03-23T06:28:00", "text": "Great news, @eid_4eec2a5a! Can you remind us what the root cause was?", "utterranceID": "20270322-1-1c49d"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270322-1-1c49d"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4eec2a5a", "timestamp": "2027-03-23T06:29:00", "text": "Sure, George. The root cause was a misconfiguration in the access control logic within the query execution pipeline. It wasn't properly verifying user permissions, which allowed unauthorized users to access restricted data.", "utterranceID": "20270322-2-ebec9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270322-2-ebec9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6d14c4ec", "timestamp": "2027-03-23T06:32:00", "text": "Thanks for the update, Alice. How did you manage to fix it?", "utterranceID": "20270322-3-a38ef"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270322-3-a38ef"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4eec2a5a", "timestamp": "2027-03-23T06:33:00", "text": "To resolve the issue, I updated the access control logic to ensure that user permissions are checked before any query execution. I also added additional unit tests to cover various permission scenarios to prevent similar issues in the future.", "utterranceID": "20270322-4-50e10"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270322-4-50e10"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-force-0527c3"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_b20b58ad", "timestamp": "2027-03-23T06:36:00", "text": "Nice work, Alice! Adding those tests will definitely help us catch any similar issues early on.", "utterranceID": "20270322-5-471c7"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270322-5-471c7"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_681e9def", "timestamp": "2027-01-05T23:58:00", "text": "Alright, I've gone through the changes. The schema updates look solid, and I see you've added the necessary fields for the training data. Nice work! 👍", "utterranceID": "20270107-3-de89b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-3-de89b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4eec2a5a", "timestamp": "2027-01-06T00:03:00", "text": "I just finished reviewing the migration scripts. They seem well-structured and tested. I ran them locally, and everything transitioned smoothly. Great job, @eid_e5715d9e! 👏", "utterranceID": "20270107-4-2ce73"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-4-2ce73"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_681e9def", "timestamp": "2027-01-06T00:06:00", "text": "Also, I checked the database performance metrics, and there's no noticeable degradation. Everything seems to be in order. 😊", "utterranceID": "20270107-5-02215"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-5-02215"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_4eec2a5a", "timestamp": "2027-01-06T00:08:00", "text": "Agreed, the performance is stable. LGTM, approved! ✅", "utterranceID": "20270107-6-7001e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-6-7001e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_681e9def", "timestamp": "2027-01-06T00:10:00", "text": "Same here, LGTM, approved! Let's get this merged. 🎉", "utterranceID": "20270107-7-56b1e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-7-56b1e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e5715d9e", "timestamp": "2027-01-06T00:12:00", "text": "Thanks, @Bob Miller and Alice! Appreciate the quick review and feedback. I'll proceed with the merge. 🙌", "utterranceID": "20270107-8-ecd35"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-8-ecd35"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_13786f09", "timestamp": "2027-01-07T14:11:00", "text": "Hi team, I wanted to discuss some open-source projects that have implemented features similar to our proposed context-aware search queries. Let's see what we can learn from them! 😊", "utterranceID": "20270107-0-fa3bb"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-0-fa3bb"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_13786f09", "timestamp": "2027-01-07T14:13:00", "text": "First up, we have Elasticsearch's 'Session-Based Query Optimization'. This feature enhances query performance by using user session data to prioritize relevant indices. Check it out here: https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/pull/4018. What do you think, @eid_b20b58ad?", "utterranceID": "20270107-1-e26e0"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-1-e26e0"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_b20b58ad", "timestamp": "2027-01-07T14:16:00", "text": "Thanks, Alice! This is interesting. Prioritizing indices based on session data could really speed up our search results. It seems like a smart way to handle large datasets. We should definitely consider this approach. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20270107-2-8ef13"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-2-8ef13"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_681e9def", "timestamp": "2027-01-07T14:19:00", "text": "Agreed, Julia. It might also help us reduce the load on our servers by focusing on the most relevant data first. I wonder how complex the implementation would be for our system. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20270107-3-d039c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-3-d039c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_13786f09", "timestamp": "2027-01-07T14:22:00", "text": "Great points! Next, let's look at Apache Solr's 'Contextual Search Enhancements'. This feature uses session metadata to refine result accuracy. Here's the link: https://github.com/apache/solr/pull/4019. Thoughts, Bob?", "utterranceID": "20270107-4-0ea44"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-4-0ea44"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_681e9def", "timestamp": "2027-01-07T14:23:00", "text": "This one seems to align closely with what we're aiming for. Using session metadata could really personalize the search experience for users. It might be worth diving deeper into their implementation to see how we can adapt it. 👍", "utterranceID": "20270107-5-f0a8b"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-5-f0a8b"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidwilliams-SearchForce", "channelID": "ch-shaix-a65760"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_b20b58ad", "timestamp": "2027-01-07T14:25:00", "text": "Yeah, I like the idea of refining accuracy with session data. It could make our search results much more relevant. Maybe we can combine some of these ideas with our existing algorithms.", "utterranceID": "20270107-6-54933"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270107-6-54933"}

{"Channel": {"name": "planning-shAIX", "channelID": "ch-shaix-1539d5"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_efc9418c", "timestamp": "2026-09-02T11:39:00", "text": "Thanks, everyone. Once we've reviewed these, let's regroup to discuss any potential improvements or issues we might foresee.", "utterranceID": "20260902-6-4c843"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260902-6-4c843"}
