{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_435d10af", "timestamp": "2026-07-23T08:47:00", "text": "Hi team, I noticed that PR# 3, which integrates the BERT model for sentiment analysis, is approved but not merged yet. Given the recent change in product direction, should we consider not merging it?", "utterranceID": "20260722-0-20eee"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260722-0-20eee"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_bf7c4dae", "timestamp": "2026-07-23T08:51:00", "text": "Hey everyone, I approved the PR earlier because it seemed aligned with our goals at the time. Can someone clarify what the new product direction is and why this PR might be unnecessary now?", "utterranceID": "20260722-1-69b0c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260722-1-69b0c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_6aaf9156", "timestamp": "2026-07-23T08:53:00", "text": "Good question. From what I understand, we're shifting focus away from enhancing sentiment analysis and more towards improving data visualization features. The BERT integration might not be relevant anymore.", "utterranceID": "20260722-2-b535c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260722-2-b535c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_374a009b", "timestamp": "2026-07-23T08:55:00", "text": "That makes sense. If sentiment analysis isn't a priority, maintaining the BERT integration could be an unnecessary overhead.", "utterranceID": "20260722-3-43ab9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260722-3-43ab9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_88c661bc", "timestamp": "2026-07-23T08:58:00", "text": "Hi all, thanks for the update. I authored the PR when sentiment analysis was a key focus. If the direction has changed, I agree it might not be needed.", "utterranceID": "20260722-4-8a2b2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260722-4-8a2b2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_798684b4", "timestamp": "2026-07-23T09:03:00", "text": "Just to confirm, has the PR been merged yet? If not, it might be easier to just not merge it.", "utterranceID": "20260722-5-f1a30"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260722-5-f1a30"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_88c661bc", "timestamp": "2026-07-23T09:05:00", "text": "No, it hasn't been merged yet. It's still open.", "utterranceID": "20260722-6-a95e2"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260722-6-a95e2"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_7c6dd6a6", "timestamp": "2026-07-23T09:10:00", "text": "In that case, I suggest we hold off on merging it. @eid_88c661bc, could you ensure it stays unmerged for now?", "utterranceID": "20260722-7-e48dc"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260722-7-e48dc"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_88c661bc", "timestamp": "2026-07-23T09:12:00", "text": "Sure, I'll make sure it remains unmerged. I'll take the necessary action soon. Thanks for the heads-up, everyone.", "utterranceID": "20260722-8-c938e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260722-8-c938e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_c7622c8e", "timestamp": "2026-07-23T09:17:00", "text": "Thanks, @eid_88c661bc. Let's keep monitoring our priorities and adjust as needed.", "utterranceID": "20260722-9-506a8"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260722-9-506a8"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_88c661bc", "timestamp": "2026-08-03T11:40:00", "text": "Hi team, I came across some interesting open-source features that might help us with our BERT fine-tuning for the finance sector. Let's take a look and see if we can draw any inspiration! 😊", "utterranceID": "20260803-0-059bf"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260803-0-059bf"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_88c661bc", "timestamp": "2026-08-03T11:42:00", "text": "First up, there's a PR from Hugging Face Transformers where they fine-tuned GPT-3 for the healthcare sector. They used healthcare-specific data to enhance medical text generation and comprehension. Here's the link: https://github.com/huggingface/transformers/pull/3385", "utterranceID": "20260803-1-58a9e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260803-1-58a9e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_259474bc", "timestamp": "2026-08-03T11:45:00", "text": "That sounds pretty relevant! Fine-tuning with domain-specific data seems to be a common approach. We could definitely consider a similar strategy for our finance data. @eid_bf7c4dae, what do you think?", "utterranceID": "20260803-2-bee7e"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260803-2-bee7e"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-fionajones-KnowledgeForce", "channelID": "ch-force-b96ca0"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_bf7c4dae", "timestamp": "2026-08-03T11:47:00", "text": "Absolutely, Julia M! Leveraging domain-specific data could really boost our sentiment analysis accuracy. Plus, Hugging Face is a solid reference point. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260803-3-8a631"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260803-3-8a631"}

{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidgarcia-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-08262e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e3c15ff5", "timestamp": "2026-06-07T07:57:00", "text": "Thanks, Fiona! This sounds quite aligned with what we're aiming for. Elasticsearch's approach to using vector embeddings could definitely enhance our ranking algorithm. I think we should consider how they handle vector similarity and scoring. 👍", "utterranceID": "20260607-2-d7c04"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260607-2-d7c04"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidgarcia-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-08262e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_515ae627", "timestamp": "2026-06-07T07:59:00", "text": "Agreed, Fiona M. Elasticsearch is known for its robust search capabilities. Their vector-based scoring could provide us with some valuable insights, especially in terms of performance optimization. 🚀", "utterranceID": "20260607-3-2f081"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260607-3-2f081"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidgarcia-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-08262e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_03a183c9", "timestamp": "2026-06-07T08:03:00", "text": "Great points! Next, let's look at Apache Solr's 'Semantic Query Expansion'. This feature expands user queries semantically using vector embeddings for better search accuracy. Here's the link: https://github.com/apache/lucene-solr/pull/3485. Thoughts, Bob?", "utterranceID": "20260607-4-78fb1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260607-4-78fb1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidgarcia-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-08262e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_515ae627", "timestamp": "2026-06-07T08:05:00", "text": "The semantic query expansion is interesting. It could help us in understanding user intent better and refining search results. However, we need to ensure it doesn't overcomplicate our current search logic. 🤔", "utterranceID": "20260607-5-0aa50"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260607-5-0aa50"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidgarcia-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-08262e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e3c15ff5", "timestamp": "2026-06-07T08:06:00", "text": "I agree with Bob. While it's a powerful feature, we should evaluate how it fits with our existing architecture. Maybe we can adapt some parts of it without a complete overhaul. @eid_03a183c9, could you look into this further?", "utterranceID": "20260607-6-c34c1"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260607-6-c34c1"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidgarcia-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-08262e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_03a183c9", "timestamp": "2026-06-07T08:08:00", "text": "Sure thing, I'll dive deeper into Solr's implementation and see how we can leverage it. Lastly, let's discuss Haystack's 'Contextual Answer Ranking'. This feature uses contextual embeddings to prioritize the most relevant answers in search results. Check it out here: https://github.com/deepset-ai/haystack/pull/3486.", "utterranceID": "20260607-7-5f3cf"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260607-7-5f3cf"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidgarcia-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-08262e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_e3c15ff5", "timestamp": "2026-06-07T08:11:00", "text": "Haystack's approach to contextual ranking is quite innovative. It could be particularly useful for our discussion threads and message prioritization. We should definitely consider how they integrate contextual embeddings. 🔍", "utterranceID": "20260607-8-5c2fd"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260607-8-5c2fd"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidgarcia-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-08262e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_515ae627", "timestamp": "2026-06-07T08:12:00", "text": "Absolutely, Fiona B. Contextual understanding is key for relevance. If we can incorporate some of their techniques, it could significantly enhance user experience. Let's keep this on our radar. 📈", "utterranceID": "20260607-9-1c3d8"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260607-9-1c3d8"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidgarcia-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-08262e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_03a183c9", "timestamp": "2026-06-07T08:15:00", "text": "Awesome insights, team! I'll compile our thoughts and start drafting a plan to integrate some of these ideas into our feature. Thanks for the great discussion! 🙌", "utterranceID": "20260607-10-0be86"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260607-10-0be86"}
{"Channel": {"name": "develop-davidgarcia-SearchFlow", "channelID": "ch-hflow-08262e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_03a183c9", "timestamp": "2026-06-08T10:16:00", "text": "Hi team, please check my PR for the new feature: Implement Semantic Search Result Ranking. Here's the link: https://github.com/salesforce/SearchFlow/pull/20. This PR includes a ranking algorithm based on vector similarity scores to ensure the most relevant messages, files, and discussions are surfaced. Let me know your thoughts! 😊", "utterranceID": "20260609-0-9e1fd"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20260609-0-9e1fd"}

{"title": "Implement Lazy Loading for Data-Heavy Components", "summary": "Introduce lazy loading for components that handle large datasets to improve performance and user experience. Ensure that components load data only when needed.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/KnowledgeForce/pull/19", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "False", "number": "19", "state": "open", "user": {"login": "eid_6aaf9156"}, "created_at": "2026-09-18T22:15:00", "reviews": [{"state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "user": {"login": "eid_2471d598"}, "comment": "The lazy loading implementation is solid for most components, but the 'UserDashboard' component still loads all data upfront. Please adjust it to load data only when the user navigates to it.", "submitted_at": "2026-09-19T03:47:00"}, {"state": "PENDING", "user": {"login": "eid_524f697b"}, "comment": "There's a noticeable improvement in load times for most components, but the 'Reports' section still seems sluggish. Consider optimizing the data fetching strategy there.", "submitted_at": "2026-09-19T03:51:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_KnowledgeForce_pull_19"}
{"title": "Schedule and Document Knowledge-Sharing Sessions", "summary": "This PR organizes knowledge-sharing sessions for the team to learn about blockchain integration and Hyperledger Fabric. It includes a schedule, presentation materials, and documentation of the sessions.", "link": "https://github.com/salesforce/KnowledgeForce/pull/20", "mergeable": "True", "merged": "False", "number": "20", "state": "open", "user": {"login": "eid_5782059f"}, "created_at": "2026-09-21T15:40:00", "reviews": [{"state": "CHANGES_REQUESTED", "user": {"login": "eid_01942cf0"}, "comment": "The schedule and presentation materials are well-prepared. However, consider adding more detailed notes or summaries for each session to assist with onboarding new team members.", "submitted_at": "2026-09-21T23:14:00"}, {"state": "PENDING", "user": {"login": "eid_0f6b0aea"}, "comment": "The schedule and materials are on point, but the session documentation needs more detail to be helpful for newcomers. Please expand on the documentation.", "submitted_at": "2026-09-21T23:09:00"}], "id": "github_com_salesforce_KnowledgeForce_pull_20"}
