{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-force-3aa08e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_8d6fe78d", "timestamp": "2027-01-31T22:08:00", "text": "Thanks, team! I'll keep you posted on both issues. Let's make sure our customers are happy. 😊", "utterranceID": "20270131-9-99df9"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270131-9-99df9"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-force-3aa08e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_fa16fefb", "timestamp": "2027-02-04T05:08:00", "text": "Hi team, I found some interesting open-source bugs that might help us with our current issues. Let's take a look and see what we can learn! 🚀", "utterranceID": "20270204-0-7366c"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270204-0-7366c"}
{"Channel": {"name": "bug-juliataylor-ContextForce", "channelID": "ch-force-3aa08e"}, "Message": {"User": {"userId": "eid_fa16fefb", "timestamp": "2027-02-04T05:13:00", "text": "First up, we have a bug in Apache Kafka related to 'Time-Series Data Misinterpretation in Streams'. It seems there's an issue with incorrect time-window aggregation leading to misleading analytics results. Here's the PR link: https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/1967. @eid_8d6fe78d, this sounds similar to the Temporal Data Misinterpretation issue you're working on. Thoughts?", "utterranceID": "20270204-1-61e69"}, "Reactions": []}, "ThreadReplies": [], "id": "20270204-1-61e69"}

